{% comment %}
  OB: a collection's ancestors in the main navigation, so a breadcrumb can
  show where a category sits (Home › Schoenen › Ballerina's) without inventing
  a collection hierarchy Shopify doesn't have. Shared by the collection hero
  (visible trail) and the PDP breadcrumb (BreadcrumbList JSON-LD).

  Rules (see the ob-collection-hero spec):
  - The first occurrence in menu order wins. Brands listed under both an
    occasion parent and Merken take the occasion parent, and menu order alone
    decides it.
  - A child whose url equals its parent's is the "Alles voor …" self-link, not
    an occurrence, so it is skipped.
  - Matched on the linked collection's handle, not the url, so a locale prefix
    (/en/collections/…) can't cause a miss.
  - A top-level match, or no match, emits nothing: the caller renders
    Home › title.

  Outputs only the ancestors, never the collection itself.

  Accepts:
  - for_collection: {Object} the collection to place
  - format: {String} 'html' (default) | 'jsonld'
  - link_class / sep_class: {String} html format: classes for each ancestor
    link and the chevron after it
  - start: {Number} jsonld format: position of the first emitted ListItem.
    Each item is followed by a comma, so the caller appends the rest.

  Usage:
  {% render 'ob-menu-trail', for_collection: collection, link_class: 'x__link', sep_class: 'x__sep' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign ob_target = for_collection.handle
  assign ob_found = false
  assign ob_depth = 0

  if ob_target != blank
    for ob_l1 in linklists['main-menu'].links
      if ob_l1.type == 'collection_link' and ob_l1.object.handle == ob_target
        assign ob_found = true
        assign ob_depth = 1
        break
      endif

      for ob_l2 in ob_l1.links
        if ob_l2.url == ob_l1.url
          continue
        endif
        if ob_l2.type == 'collection_link' and ob_l2.object.handle == ob_target
          assign ob_found = true
          assign ob_a1 = ob_l1
          assign ob_depth = 2
          break
        endif

        for ob_l3 in ob_l2.links
          if ob_l3.url == ob_l2.url
            continue
          endif
          if ob_l3.type == 'collection_link' and ob_l3.object.handle == ob_target
            assign ob_found = true
            assign ob_a1 = ob_l1
            assign ob_a2 = ob_l2
            assign ob_depth = 3
            break
          endif
        endfor

        if ob_found
          break
        endif
      endfor

      if ob_found
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign ob_position = start | default: 1
-%}

{%- if ob_depth > 1 -%}
  {%- if format == 'jsonld' -%}
    {"@type":"ListItem","position":{{ ob_position }},"name":{{ ob_a1.title | json }},"item":{{ shop.url | append: ob_a1.url | json }}},
    {%- if ob_depth == 3 -%}
      {"@type":"ListItem","position":{{ ob_position | plus: 1 }},"name":{{ ob_a2.title | json }},"item":{{ shop.url | append: ob_a2.url | json }}},
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    <a class="{{ link_class }}" href="{{ ob_a1.url }}">{{ ob_a1.title | escape }}</a>
    {%- render 'ob-icon', icon: 'chevron-right', class: sep_class -%}
    {%- if ob_depth == 3 -%}
      <a class="{{ link_class }}" href="{{ ob_a2.url }}">{{ ob_a2.title | escape }}</a>
      {%- render 'ob-icon', icon: 'chevron-right', class: sep_class -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
